hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"161","On the authority of Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: We returned with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was traveling from Mecca to Medina, until when we were on the road with water, a group of people hurried in the afternoon and performed ablution while they were... Calves, so we came to them and their heels were white, shining, untouched by water, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire! “Perform ablution well.”"
"162","We are Ahmed bin Abda, we are Abdul Aziz Al-Darawardi. H Yusuf bin Musa, narrated by Jarir, both of them, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Woe to the heels of the Fire.”"
